                <pb facs="0456" n="338" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg338"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/43: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-03T17:00:00-06:00">March 3, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:04 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>46. I am informed by Estrada that the garrison at Vera Cruz, commanded by General
                    Aguirre, has risen and that there is an uprising in Sonora presumably headed by
                    General Manzo.</p>
                <p>The Government has closed the ports of Vera Cruz and Nogales to prevent the entry
                    of arms and munitions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morrow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
